# Unicode CLDR, locale ta, dateFields.json, field day.
# A counted noun is CASE-MARKED in Tamil, not bare: the ago pattern is
# the DATIVE unit plus முன், and the in-N pattern is the LOCATIVE on
# the unit with no preposition at all.  Both case forms are unit
# surfaces in their own right, and both are CLDR's own wording.
# The plural stem is suppletive in shape (நாள் -> நாட்கள்).  நாள் and
# நாளை (tomorrow) differ by one grapheme and both stand next to a
# numeral, so the day-word file carries only the unit senses.
நாள்
நாட்கள்
நாளுக்கு
நாட்களுக்கு
